  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA broad upper trough is expected to advance eastward today, as \nanother trough across the Tennessee Valley drifts northward. \nIncreasing moisture and diurnally driven instability should \nresult in scattered showers and thunderstorms development by the\nafternoon. ML CAPE is progged to be around 1000 j/kg, with weak\nshear (10-20kt) in place. While overall severe storm potential\nis limited, a few gusty storms with heavy downpours will be\npossible. The southern stream low is progged to phase with the \napproaching trough tonight. Moisture and limited shortwave \nsupported lift should still result in scattered showers across \nthe area, with a thunderstorm still possible with limited \nelevated instability. \n\nAnother shortwave embedded in the broad upper trough is progged\nto track across the region on Thursday, with additional showers\nand thunderstorms. Instability and shear values are expected to\nbe similar to today, with a similar message of possible gusty\nthunderstorms and heavy downpours. This activity should again\ndiminish after sunset, though scattered showers/isolated storms\nare still expected. Existing cloud cover will have an impact on\nthe amount of diurnally driven instability. \n\nA stronger shortwave is progged for a Friday passage, with\nhigher chances for showers and thunderstorms. Instability is\nprogged to be slightly higher, with an ML CAPE around 1500 j/kg,\nwith similar 0-6km shear around 20kt. More uncertainty in\nshortwave location and timing exists over the weekend. In\ngeneral, broad upper troughing and surface heating should result\nin daily scattered shower/storm chances. Another strong\nshortwave and cold front approach and passage is indicated for\nMonday into Tuesday in model ensembles, with continued\nshowers and thunderstorms. \n\nOverall uncertainty exists in the daily chances for severe\nstorms and locally heavy rainfall. This potential will depend on\nthe amount of cloud cover, surface heating, outflows from\nprevious convection, etc. At this time the overall potential for\nsevere storms and flooding through the weekend is low. This will\nbe monitored over the upcoming days for any increase in\npotential of thunderstorm hazards.",
